// TEST: Compact Partial Read (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
// ERROR-CONTAINS: partial read of a compact
// ============================================================================
// `S` is a rank-2 symmetric result: ONE compact record spanning TWO
// coordinates. Counting one argument against one record classified `S(1)`
// as a full scalar read, and the emitted `double x = S[1L]` was a row
// pointer. Coordinates are walked through the records in flat order; a
// count that lands inside a compact group has no residual class, the same
// refusal the wildcard form gives.
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let S = method_for(A, A) <@> (+) |> compute
let x = S(1)
